# Checkpoint C pre-screen (slice 1, venue tripwire) -- read-only, Opus

## SUMMARY
- **Slice 1 newly holds 45 clean shows (27 delivered, 18 packaged... see table): 28 by 1d only (A), 13 by step-1 `venue mismatch` only (B), 4 by both.** Only 3 are TRUE: ginblossoms-2003-01-24 and stuallenandmarshotel-2012-11-11 (two performances; the shipped venue is WRONG today), plus ryanadams-2007-06-06 (right hold, wrong reason: the city test fails only on England/UK). **42 are FALSE.**
- FALSE causes, A: country name/code not folded (6: GER/DE/AU/DK/UK/England), suburb/neighbourhood/landmark vs metro, no alias (10), comma-less 'City ST' (4), venue text or junk in the city field (3), 3-field/semicolon regions (2), diacritic (1), 'NY, NY' (1), region typo (1). B: step 1 now demands compatible cities but prev never checked them: country forms (3), jerrybase 'Jersey City, NY' data error (3), Hebron vs Thornville alias gap (3), suburb/neighbouring town (2), unknown archive city (1, spec-mandated), 'NV/Clark County' region (1).
- 32 of the 45 would get a SHIPPED venue/city string change on any future redo/fix (1d ships the selected recording's strings); 14 of those are regressions (misspellings, lowercase, junk: a date as city, venue text in city, 'Hamilton Ontario, CA'). reapply does not touch them (held-only), but the next redo/fix would hold them.
- **Recommendation: narrow before approving.** Two small changes, measured with a validated simulator over the whole library:
  - **V: 1d fires only when the selected recording's venue is NOT venues_equivalent to the vote's** (same hall + 'different' city is locality noise, not a second performance). Fixes 23/45, keeps all 3 TRUE held, removes 1d on 35 shows library-wide, adds none; also stops gomez-2006-10-06 shipping a WRONG 'Boston, MA' for the Bowery Ballroom. DSO-2003-01-25 stays held.
  - **S: step 1 passes on venue equivalence alone when the pair was already equivalent under the pre-slice rule** (prev never checked cities there; keep the city check only for pairs newly equivalent via 1b). Fixes 13/45 (all B), removes the slice-1-added step-1 flag on 26 shows, none of which base flagged; only gratefuldead-1972-04-26 (newly equivalent Jahrhundert Halle) differs from dropping the check outright, and stays held.
  - **V+S: 39/45 cleared; the 6 left held = 3 TRUE + 3 FALSE** (beneventorusso-2005-08-27, gratefuldead-1978-09-16, smashingpumpkins-1997-06-28; venue names differ). Country/region folding (C or R) adds 2 more but releases the ryanadams-2007-06-06 catch; the metro class (~15) cannot be fixed with a bounded alias table. Not recommended now.
- Items 1-5:
  1. PASS with notes. 74 cleared pairs: 35 step 1 (30 spelling-only, 5 different-name via the university strip, all verdicts correct), 4 swaps, 34 1c, 1 1a. 1c shipped strings: 29 right/acceptable, 4 need --set-venue (DSO-2005-06-07, DSO-2005-07-17 guest annotations; DSO-2017-06-27 wrong name; philleshandfriends-1999-10-31 'University Of Illinois' = UIC Pavilion), 1 less precise (GD-1991-10-31). 2 of 4 swaps ship a worse string than the vote (GD-1978-04-15, GD-1985-06-14). The 3 known wrong strings did not clear (two-venue signature).
  2. PASS. 38/38 swap/1c shows have compatible cities (re-derived); all 36 step-1/1a clears too.
  3. PASS. darkstarorchestra-2003-01-25: venue 'Barrymore Theater', city Madison, WI, held by 1d (`city` family). gratefuldead-1978-11-17 keeps `venue mismatch`.
  4. PASS (mechanically): 66 string changes, each carries a swap/1c note or 1d flag; step 1/1a/1b changed none. 4b: 2 clears with shipped venue not equivalent to the selected one, both benign. But 26 of the 66 new strings are junk/regressions or TRUE conflicts, flagged in list 4a.
  5. Bottom 10 1c by token overlap: 8 festival/site or vague names (all right except philleshandfriends-1999-10-31), plus 2 Greek Theatre/Mexicali rows; DSO-2005-06-07 needs --set-venue.
- Row counts (flagged/routine): list 1 43/31; list 2 2/36; list 3 0/2; list 4a 36/30; list 4b 0/2; list 5 10/0. Newly-held: 45 rows (3 TRUE, 42 FALSE), all for decision. Held shows gaining a slice-1 flag: 33 (6 TRUE).
